Revision: 395
Author:   al...@bedatadriven.com
Date:     Sun Nov 20 14:51:16 2011
Log:      Started some refactoring around Builders. Have been doing some
testing on largish
benchmarks and there are a couple places where element-by-element
incremental allocation
just kills the whole thing. In most of these cases, we know the total
allocation needed
any of time, and we will have to be better about specifying it up front. So
now there is a
new Vector.newBuilderWithInitialCapacity(n) that should be preferred to
newBuilder()

The NamesBuilder helper class has also been added, which is smart about not
allocating memory
for the names vector unless it is actually used.

http://code.google.com/p/renjin/source/detail?r=395

